// Crash-reporting configuration for the SenseBridge app target.
//
// Committed, and deliberately sets no DSN of its own. Chained in from
// `Signing.xcconfig` because Xcode allows a target exactly one config file per
// build configuration, and that one is already spoken for — this is the rest of
// that file's job, split out so a file named "Signing" is only ever about
// signing.
//
// A Sentry DSN is not a secret: it is a write-only ingest endpoint, it ships
// inside the app bundle by necessity, and it cannot be used to read anything
// out of a Sentry project. It is still left empty here for the same reason
// `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` is — it identifies *one* project's Sentry org, and a fork
// that inherited it would silently post its crashes into this project's issue
// stream.
//
// Put your own in `Sentry.local.xcconfig`, which is gitignored:
//
//     SENTRY_DSN = https:/$()/<key>@<org-id>.ingest.us.sentry.io/<project-id>
//
// The `/$()/` is not a typo and is not optional. Xcode's xcconfig parser treats
// `//` as the start of a comment *anywhere* on a line, including inside a URL,
// so a DSN pasted verbatim silently truncates to `https:` and the app reports
// nowhere. `$()` expands to nothing and breaks up the `//` so the parser never
// sees it. This is the single most common way to get this wrong.
//
// With no local file, `SENTRY_DSN` stays empty, `Info.plist` carries an empty
// `SentryDSN`, and `CrashReporting.start` returns without initialising the SDK.
// A fresh clone therefore builds, runs, and passes its tests with crash
// reporting simply absent — never half-configured.
//
// Configuring a DSN does *not* by itself send anything. Reporting also requires
// the user to switch on Settings → Diagnostics → "Send crash reports", which is
// off by default and is the actual consent gate. See CrashReporting.swift and
// docs/PRIVACY.md.
//
// It can also be set for a single command, which is how CI would do it without
// writing a file:
//
//     xcodebuild SENTRY_DSN=https:/$()/... ...
SENTRY_DSN =

#include? "Sentry.local.xcconfig"
